  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The initial configuration of the system is as shown in the figure.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/260423_qrghu.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 144px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rThe string and the pulley are light. The bob is released and the string starts wrapping around the pulley. (The pulley is held in place by a force applied at the centre)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/jee_2phy.JPG\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 152px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rFind the rate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> at which the length of the string wrapped around the pulley increases (as a function of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>).</p>\r",
    "image": null
